{
	"name": "AI captions from a sheet to sprkly, held for approval",
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "ddbc580c-4c59-48ac-b39d-046befdef675",
			"name": "Overview",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [
				-1000,
				-80
			],
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Turn topic ideas into posts, checked by you\n\n### How it works\n- Every hour it reads the rows with Status **Idea**.\n- OpenAI writes two captions per topic: a short one and a long one.\n- sprkly schedules the short caption to your X, Threads and Bluesky accounts, and the long caption to your LinkedIn, Facebook and Instagram accounts.\n- Every post has **Requires Approval** on. sprkly emails you an Approve link, and nothing goes out until you click it.\n- The AI lives in OpenAI. sprkly has no AI. It only publishes.\n- The row gets both post IDs, or the reason it failed. When a post goes out, its link lands in the row.\n\n### Setup\n- Needs the n8n-nodes-sprkly community node (Settings, Community Nodes).\n- Logins: a sprkly API key, a Google login, an OpenAI key.\n- Sheet columns: Row ID, Status, Topic, Schedule Time, Short Accounts, Long Accounts, Image URL, Short Post ID, Long Post ID, Short Link, Long Link, Error.\n- Accounts look like `x:myhandle, threads:myhandle`.\n- Instagram needs an image. Put a link in Image URL, or leave Instagram out.\n- Pick your sheet in each of the 4 sheet nodes.\n- sprkly API docs: https://sprkly.app/docs/api\n- Node: https://github.com/ahlanlhw/n8n-nodes-sprkly\n\n### Customize\n- Change the voice in **Write both captions**.",
				"height": 880,
				"width": 520,
				"color": 1
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "8da6a13a-a1cc-4dcd-b70c-1c2e98e48aee",
			"name": "Note: write and schedule",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [
				-440,
				80
			],
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Write, then hold for approval\nOpenAI writes the captions. Each sprkly node makes the posts with Requires Approval on, and an External ID from the Row ID, so a re-run never posts twice. Set a time far enough ahead to approve it.",
				"height": 560,
				"width": 1500,
				"color": 7
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "d455d280-1fea-4360-b7ec-d5dc2fe3b886",
			"name": "Note: track posts",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [
				-440,
				720
			],
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Track what went out\nWhen an approved post goes out or fails, its link or the reason lands in the row. The row is found by its Row ID.",
				"height": 440,
				"width": 1080,
				"color": 7
			}
		},
